{"type":"text","timestamp":1791836959582,"sessionID":"ses_ece31f884ffecanusyIJunY46W","part":{"id":"prt_131ce1db3001261rwmFeuG4IQe","sessionID":"ses_ece31f884ffecanusyIJunY46W","messageID":"msg_131ce1971001dPjPIb2yBAklhC","type":"text","text":"Now I have all the reference material I need. Let me analyze the source request and produce the full Requirements Elicitation Package.\n\n**Source request analysis:**\n\n> \"While a batch is in validation mode, when the operator submits it, the batch service shall validate every record and notify the operator if any record is invalid.\"\n\nThis contains:\n- A state (`batch is in validation mode`)\n- A trigger (`operator submits it`)\n- Two responses joined by `and`: (1) validate every record, (2) notify the operator if any record is invalid\n- The second response is itself conditional on an unwanted condition\n\nThese two responses must be split: the validation obligation and the notification obligation are independently testable. The notification path is also an unwanted/conditional behavior that deserves its own `If … then` candidate.\n\nLet me now draft the full package and write it to `artifacts/result.md`.","time":{"start":1791836954035,"end":1791836959582}}}
